  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Default List",
      "code": "<Content>\n  <OrderedList>\n    <ListItem>First item</ListItem>\n    <ListItem>Second item</ListItem>\n    <ListItem>Third item</ListItem>\n  </OrderedList>\n</Content>"
    },
    {
      "title": "Alphabetic Lowercase",
      "code": "<Content>\n  <OrderedList type=\"a\">\n    <ListItem>First item</ListItem>\n    <ListItem>Second item</ListItem>\n    <ListItem>Third item</ListItem>\n  </OrderedList>\n</Content>"
    },
    {
      "title": "Alphabetic Uppercase",
      "code": "<Content>\n  <OrderedList type=\"A\">\n    <ListItem>First item</ListItem>\n    <ListItem>Second item</ListItem>\n    <ListItem>Third item</ListItem>\n  </OrderedList>\n</Content>"
    },
    {
      "title": "Roman Numerals",
      "code": "<Content>\n  <OrderedList type=\"I\">\n    <ListItem>First item</ListItem>\n    <ListItem>Second item</ListItem>\n    <ListItem>Third item</ListItem>\n  </OrderedList>\n</Content>"
    },
    {
      "title": "Custom Starting Number",
      "code": "<Content>\n  <OrderedList start={5}>\n    <ListItem>Fifth item</ListItem>\n    <ListItem>Sixth item</ListItem>\n    <ListItem>Seventh item</ListItem>\n  </OrderedList>\n</Content>"
    },
    {
      "title": "Reversed Order",
      "code": "<Content>\n  <OrderedList reversed>\n    <ListItem>Third item (shown as 3)</ListItem>\n    <ListItem>Second item (shown as 2)</ListItem>\n    <ListItem>First item (shown as 1)</ListItem>\n  </OrderedList>\n</Content>"
    },
    {
      "title": "Colored List",
      "code": "<Content>\n  <OrderedList textColor=\"primary\">\n    <ListItem>First item</ListItem>\n    <ListItem>Second item</ListItem>\n    <ListItem>Third item</ListItem>\n  </OrderedList>\n</Content>"
    },
    {
      "title": "Nested Lists",
      "code": "<Content>\n  <OrderedList>\n    <ListItem>First item</ListItem>\n    <ListItem>\n      Second item with nested list\n      <OrderedList type=\"a\">\n        <ListItem>Nested item a</ListItem>\n        <ListItem>Nested item b</ListItem>\n      </OrderedList>\n    </ListItem>\n    <ListItem>Third item</ListItem>\n  </OrderedList>\n</Content>"
    },
    {
      "title": "Compound (dot-notation) usage",
      "code": "<Content>\n  <OrderedList>\n    <OrderedList.Item>First item</OrderedList.Item>\n    <OrderedList.Item>Second item</OrderedList.Item>\n  </OrderedList>\n</Content>"
    }
  ],
  "accessibility": "- **List Structure:** Screen readers announce ordered lists with their numbering, helping users understand sequential content.\n- **Semantic Markup:** Using proper `<ol>` and `<li>` elements ensures accessibility for all users.\n- **Numbering Type:** The `type` attribute is announced by most screen readers, providing context about the list format.\n\n:::info\nUse `OrderedList` when the order of items is significant, such as steps in a process or ranked items.\n:::",
